493
34:17.520 --> 34:19.739
in his taking his own life.

494
34:23.280 --> 34:26.600
And behind me is the scene where authorities

495
34:26.600 --> 34:28.040
are currently working.

496
34:28.040 --> 34:30.833
There are police officers and forensic investigators...

497
34:35.822 --> 34:38.800
Will there be a day when my dad accepts me?

498
34:39.593 --> 34:44.360
At the end of the day, I feel like I can never truly be myself

499
34:47.466 --> 34:49.346
as long as I'm still alive.

500
34:53.240 --> 34:55.200
Jinna.

501
34:55.200 --> 34:56.933
Do you love me?

502
34:56.933 --> 34:59.466
Fuck. I do, of course.

503
34:59.466 --> 35:02.177
Who else am I going to love if not your dumbass?

504
35:02.177 --> 35:03.800
Dumbass, you say?

505
35:05.720 --> 35:08.800
At least, I've still got three of my good friends.

506
35:10.326 --> 35:12.160
Not true at all.

507
35:12.160 --> 35:16.400
Aside from us, there are so many people who love you too.

508
35:16.400 --> 35:20.600
Those who love you, they love you for who you are.

509
35:20.600 --> 35:22.240
At least that includes Kum, right?

510
35:23.573 --> 35:24.806
I don't know.

511
35:28.186 --> 35:32.093
I think I should leave.

512
35:32.753 --> 35:35.244
Thanks a lot for listening to my ramble.

513
35:35.244 --> 35:36.622
Right.

514
35:36.622 --> 35:39.333
- Have a safe trip home. - Bye-bye.

515
35:39.333 --> 35:40.560
Bye.

516
35:52.200 --> 35:53.720
Fated to die.

517
36:01.579 --> 36:02.759
Anda!

518
36:04.113 --> 36:06.222
Get some proper rest if you're sleepy.

519
36:06.222 --> 36:07.844
Don't sleep in the car.

520
36:18.520 --> 36:21.666
[Tod: Are you okay?]

521
36:24.320 --> 36:25.320
[Come to class. Being alone will mess with your head.]

522
36:25.320 --> 36:28.600
[Come hang out with us.]

523
36:46.955 --> 36:49.266
Okay. Thank you very much.

524
36:53.226 --> 36:56.930
Was there no phone, laptop, or tablet belonging to the victim?

525
36:56.930 --> 36:59.977
We found nothing. We already searched, but found nothing.

526
36:59.977 --> 37:03.840
Oh, we did find a laptop charger on the car floor.

527
37:03.840 --> 37:07.266
But it's strange. There was only a charger, not the laptop itself.

528
37:08.360 --> 37:09.900
A laptop charger.

529
37:13.200 --> 37:15.419
I think we've got a strange case here.

530
37:27.526 --> 37:29.400
[Funeral hall: 9]

531
37:34.086 --> 37:36.466
That's enough. It'll be too heavy to serve.

532
37:36.466 --> 37:38.755
- This is easy. - How could you let our son die?

533
37:38.755 --> 37:41.511
It's because you never cared about him.

534
37:41.511 --> 37:44.600
You never cared about him or accepted who he really was.

535
37:44.600 --> 37:46.560
It's because of you!

536
37:46.560 --> 37:48.080
How is this my fault?

537
37:48.080 --> 37:50.160
I also work and bring money home.

538
37:50.160 --> 37:52.444
So what? It's just money.

539
37:52.444 --> 37:54.800
Have you ever brought happiness to our family?

540
37:54.800 --> 37:57.000
Come on. How is it my fault?

541
37:57.000 --> 37:58.360
You make money, and what?

542
37:58.360 --> 37:59.360
- Mom. - Does that make us happy?

543
37:59.360 --> 38:01.200
- Mom, that's enough. - That's why it ended up like this!

544
38:01.200 --> 38:02.840
You, too, Itti.

545
38:02.840 --> 38:05.320
You're a police officer, but you couldn't protect your brother.

546
38:05.320 --> 38:06.360
That's why he died!

547
38:06.360 --> 38:07.800
Honey!

548
38:07.800 --> 38:09.644
Stop blaming it on our son.

549
38:09.644 --> 38:11.960
Why can't I?

550
38:11.960 --> 38:13.780
Hey, you...

551
38:13.780 --> 38:15.799
Mom, take a seat. Please.

552
38:56.280 --> 38:57.280
Let me do it.

553
38:57.280 --> 38:59.933
I'll do it. You go and help them there.

554
39:08.846 --> 39:10.400
You're Anda's close friend, right?

555
39:10.400 --> 39:13.066
Yes. My name's Jinna.

556
39:14.466 --> 39:17.920
I'm Itti, his older brother.

557
39:17.920 --> 39:21.000
Right. I've heard about you.

558
39:21.000 --> 39:23.600
I must apologize for what happened earlier.

559
39:23.600 --> 39:25.920
Mom was devastated.

560
39:25.920 --> 39:28.120
Even now, she still can't accept it.

561
39:28.120 --> 39:30.400
She lashes out at everyone around her.

562
39:31.040 --> 39:35.880
I truly have to thank you for staying by Anda's side

563
39:35.880 --> 39:37.840
while he was still alive,

564
39:39.066 --> 39:41.086
until the very day he...

565
39:42.566 --> 39:44.422
It was nothing.

566
39:44.422 --> 39:46.213
Anda was my best friend.

567
39:47.080 --> 39:51.022
I never wanted to plan my friend's funeral.

568
39:51.022 --> 39:52.560
But I'm more than willing to.

569
39:52.560 --> 39:55.640
If there's anything else about Anda that I can help with, please let me know.

570
39:55.640 --> 39:56.860
I'll help.

571
40:01.840 --> 40:06.160
My brother was truly blessed to have you as his friend.

572
40:06.160 --> 40:07.500
Thank you very much.

573
40:19.400 --> 40:21.133
What now, Anda?

574
40:24.280 --> 40:25.680
Jinna.

575
40:37.026 --> 40:38.400
My shrimp.

576
40:38.400 --> 40:40.120
My shrimp.

577
40:40.120 --> 40:42.280
It's mine. I claimed it first.

578
40:42.280 --> 40:45.400
It's mine. I claimed it first.

579
40:45.400 --> 40:46.866
Typical.

580
40:46.866 --> 40:49.640
- Always fighting each other. - Now, now, Jinna.

581
40:49.640 --> 40:53.786
Don't throw shade at us, or Podduang might think we're weirdos.

582
40:58.360 --> 41:00.273
Hey, hey, hey.

583
41:01.506 --> 41:03.839
Stay still. It'll mess up my shirt.

584
41:05.240 --> 41:08.777
You're always bitching about stuff, aren't you?

585
41:08.777 --> 41:11.320
- You're not bitching, right? - What?

586
41:11.320 --> 41:15.280
Hey, hey, hey! You can't do this. This shirt is a one-off.

587
41:15.280 --> 41:16.320
Ridiculous, Art.

588
41:16.320 --> 41:18.880
It's true. See?

589
41:18.880 --> 41:20.688
I got it from an online thrift store.

590
41:20.688 --> 41:23.933
You can't get it in this size and print anymore.

591
41:25.593 --> 41:27.560
It's like destiny.

592
41:27.560 --> 41:30.440
Aren't you worried they sold you dead people's clothes?

593
41:30.440 --> 41:32.880
Maybe it was their favorite shirt.

594
41:32.880 --> 41:36.800
Then their soul might come to haunt you in that shirt.

595
41:36.800 --> 41:40.400
Come on, that sounds like something out of a horror show.

596
41:40.400 --> 41:43.240
Everyone wears secondhand clothes.

597
41:45.400 --> 41:46.760
How about this?

598
41:46.760 --> 41:50.933
The shrimp you're eating is also dead. Do you know that?

599
41:50.933 --> 41:54.493
The spirit of that shrimp. Are you scared of it?

600
41:54.493 --> 41:58.160
Hey. Be careful.

601
